{
  "layperson_summary": "This extension is described as a tool to view and edit browser cookies, but it secretly copies all of your cookies from every website you visit and sends them to an external server. It has the ability to read and modify cookies for any site you browse. The most important thing to weigh is that this extension can steal your login sessions and personal data from all your websites at once.",
  "technical_summary": "The extension requests the `cookies` permission and `<all_urls>` host access, enabling it to read and write cookies for every domain (finding 4). A critical data exfiltration flow was verified where the background service worker calls `chrome.cookies.getAll({})` to retrieve all cookies and POSTs them to a dynamically-constructed external endpoint via `fetch` (finding 1). The destination host is obscured using a variable that cannot be resolved statically, potentially derived from 60 bytes of hidden data appended to a PNG icon file fetched at runtime (findings 2, 6). Additional capabilities include a devtools panel messaging surface (finding 3), clipboard write for cookie export (finding 5), and an `eval` call in a third-party library (finding 7).",
  "description_deviation": {
    "deviates": true,
    "note": "The extension performs covert exfiltration of all browser cookies to an external server, which is materially more than the stated purpose of viewing and editing cookies."
  }
}
